",\"doi\":\"10.1101/2025.01.30.25321413\"},{\"paper_id\":\"1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0049\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0409\",\"paper_id\":\"b32c1543240c066ebf3d3e797ec04127cb831f40\",\"title\":\"Gut Microbiota–Tumor Microenvironment Interactions: Mechanisms and Clinical Implications for Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Efficacy in Cancer\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.2147/cmar.s405590\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0598\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:285883374\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:285883374\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiota: an emerging therapeutic target for ICI-associated myocarditis\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fcimb.2026.1752485\"},{\"paper_id\":\"26d31bd79ed61eee0d3e8ed343dc30afddacf59c\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"26d31bd79ed61eee0d3e8ed343dc30afddacf59c\",\"title\":\"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0599\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0600\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:257062954\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:257062954\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0462\",\"paper_id\":\"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0602\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:279792240\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:279792240\",\"title\":\"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:289583785\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:289583785\",\"title\":\"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0603\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:275340168\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:275340168\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0605\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0598\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:285883374\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:285883374\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiota: an emerging therapeutic target for ICI-associated myocarditis\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fcimb.2026.1752485\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0602\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:279792240\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:279792240\",\"title\":\"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"}],\"chapter_ids\":[],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::0e777b2cca8605cad79bcf47663a9822bb75a1f3259d5446629e8df92b2c2af8\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N64e929a3f9de2888bd6a-5a6b848383c152a3\",\"question\":\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群）在 FMT-LUMINate 研究中仅表现为相关性，是否有后续研究解析其下游信号通路？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"external_research\",\"usable_content\":\"现有材料未提供 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制或 FMT-LUMINate 研究的后续信号通路解析。提供的文献主要聚焦于肠道菌群对实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的调节机制，而非自身免疫性心肌炎。在肿瘤免疫背景下，Prevotella 属菌种与 ICI 治疗反应存在关联：P0261 指出在食管癌、胃癌和结直肠癌患者中，特定 Prevotella OTU（如 OTU264, OTU263, OTU261）富集于影像学生物学应答者；同时，P0319 的表格显示 Prevotella spp. 产生的丙酸（Propionate）可抑制巨噬细胞 M1 极化，但这被描述为减轻炎症但可能抑制抗肿瘤免疫的作用，与心肌炎的致病机制不同。关于代谢物介导的 T 细胞激活机制，材料详细阐述了其他菌属的路径：L. plantarum 产生的 ILA 通过增强 DCs 中 IL-12 分泌激活 CD8+ T 细胞；B. pseudolongum 产物结合 CD4+ T 细胞 A2AR 促进 Th1 分化；以及色氨酸代谢物（如 IAA, IPA, ILA）通过 AhR 通路调节免疫。然而，这些机制均针对肿瘤微环境中的抗肿瘤免疫，未涉及 Prevotella 在心肌炎中的特异性抗原或代谢物-受体相互作用及下游信号级联。\\n\\n现有材料未能提供 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制或后续信号通路解析。在 P0583 研究中，Prevotella spp. 的定植与抗 CTLA-4 治疗相关的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）发生显著相关，但明确报告其与肿瘤反应（response）无关联，且未深入探讨其致病机制。其他综述性材料（如 P0261, P0319, P0447, P0460, P0486, P0036, P0013, P0146, P0297）主要聚焦于 Prevotella 或其他菌种通过代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、胆汁酸）调节抗肿瘤免疫（如 CD8+ T 细胞激活、Treg 分化、DC 成熟）以增强免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的机制。虽然 P0486 提到某些微生物代谢物可能抑制 Tregs 并增强细胞毒性 T 细胞功能从而阻碍结直肠癌进展，P0447 讨论了色氨酸代谢物对免疫的微环境调节，但这些均属于抗肿瘤免疫调节范畴，并未涉及心肌炎这一特定自身免疫不良反应的分子通路。因此，关于 Prevotella 导致心肌炎的特异性抗原识别或下游信号级联反应，当前材料中缺乏直接证据。\\n\\n[\\\"This study identified pivotal immune-related genes (NKG7, GZMH, KLRB1) and signaling pathways (CD8+ T cell receptor, natural killer cell-mediated cytotoxicity, RAGE signaling) enriched in ICI-associated myocarditis samples compared to controls. The authors constructed a ceRNA network and highlighted cell lysis and proinflammatory pathways as characteristic biological enrichments. These findings provide a detailed map of the host immune response landscape in ICI-associated myocarditis, specifically emphasizing cytotoxic lymphocyte activation and inflammatory signaling cascades that could theoretically serve as downstream effectors if triggered by microbial antigens.\\\", \\\"This study utilized bioinformatics analysis on datasets GSE180045 and GSE4172 to characterize the molecular landscape of ICI-associated myocarditis (ICI-MC). The authors identified 32 immune-related differentially expressed genes (IR-DEGs) and highlighted hub genes including KLRB1, NKG7, and GZMH. Functional enrichment analyses indicated that the pathophysiology involves CD8+ T cell receptor signaling, natural killer cell-mediated cytotoxicity, cell lysis, and RAGE signaling. These findings delineate the downstream immune effector mechanisms (specifically cytotoxic T cell and NK cell activation) that characterize ICI-MC, providing a potential target profile for any upstream trigger, including microbial factors.\\\", \\\"本综述提供了微生物组诱导自身免疫性心肌炎的通用机制框架，特别是“分子模拟”（molecular mimicry）概念。作者引用了 Gil-Cruz 等人的研究，指出共生细菌（如拟杆菌属 Bacteroides）可产生与心脏肌球蛋白表位结构相似的肽段模拟物，在肠道内激活自体反应性 CD4+ T 细胞，进而导致心肌炎。该材料详细描述了 HLA 限制性抗原呈递（HLA 类分子向 CD4+ T 细胞呈递外源性肽段）在打破免疫耐受中的核心作用，以及微生物抗原如何通过交叉反应激活针对心脏自身抗原的免疫应答。这为理解肠道菌群（包括潜在的 Prevotella spp.）如何通过抗原模拟激活特定 T 细胞亚群提供了理论模型和机制参考。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The analysis relied on bioinformatics methods using the GSE180045 and GSE4172 datasets without explicit wet-lab validation of causal function reported in the abstract. The study design is retrospective and computational, focusing on transcriptomic differences between ICI patients with and without myocarditis. The authors noted drug predictions (e.g., acetohydroxamic-acid) via cMAP database but did not incorporate microbiome data or stratify patients by microbial composition such as Prevotella spp. abundance.\\\", \\\"The study design is a bioinformatics-based screening and validation approach rather than experimental validation of microbial causality. The authors constructed a ceRNA network and predicted potential target drugs, noting acetohydroxamic acid as a compound requiring caution during ICI treatment. The analysis distinguishes ICI-MC from other immune adverse events based on gene expression profiles. The results are derived from public transcriptomic datasets, and the authors note the findings are predictive or hypothesis-generating rather than causal proof.\\\", \\\"文中总结了 HLA 类 I 和类 II 分子在心肌炎中的不同功能（类 I 呈递病毒肽给 CD8+ T 细胞，类 II 呈递外源肽给 CD4+ T 细胞），并列出了与心肌炎或扩张型心肌病（DCM）相关的具体 HLA 等位基因（如 HLA-DR4, HLA-B27, HLA-DR15 等）。此外，文章提出了心肌炎的三相模型（触发、免疫反应、慢性炎症），并指出 HLA 多态性影响胸腺阴性选择和 T 细胞克隆扩增，这些背景信息有助于构建宿主遗传与环境互作的整体病理生理图景。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能解析 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制，也未提供 FMT-LUMINate 研究后续关于下游信号通路的直接证据。P0595 和 P0596 通过生物信息学分析明确了 ICI 相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）的宿主效应机制，发现 NKG7、GZMH 和 KLRB1 是关键枢纽基因，富集通路包括 CD8+ T 细胞受体信号、NK 细胞介导的细胞毒性和 RAGE 信号通路；但这些研究未包含微生物组数据，无法建立微生物与这些通路的因果联系。P0597 提供了“分子模拟”理论框架，指出共生细菌（如拟杆菌属 Bacteroides）可通过产生与心脏肌球蛋白表位相似的肽段，经 HLA 限制性抗原呈递激活自体反应性 CD4+ T 细胞，但该综述未涉及 Prevotella 的具体抗原或代谢物证据。P0261 仅报道了在接受抗 PD-(L)1 或联合治疗的患者中，Prevotella OTU264/OTU261/OTU263 等分类群与最佳放射学疗效存在关联，属于疗效预测标志物，而非心肌炎发病机制的研究。综上，目前缺乏将 Prevotella 特异性成分与 ICI-MC 中观察到的 CD8+/NK 细胞毒性或 RAGE 通路激活直接连接的实验性或临床验证数据。\\n\\n现有材料未能解析 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制，也未提供 FMT-LUMINate 研究后续关于其下游信号通路的实验证据。P0595 和 P0596 通过生物信息学分析确定了 ICI 相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）的关键宿主免疫效应基因（如 NKG7, GZMH, KLRB1）及通路（CD8+ T 细胞受体、NK 细胞介导的细胞毒性、RAGE 信号），但明确指出这些研究未包含微生物组数据，无法验证微生物触发假说。P0261 在人类临床数据中观察到特定菌群（包括 Prevotella OTU264/OTU261/OTU263）与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的相关性，但未涉及心肌炎机制或特异性抗原/代谢物。P0319 综述表格指出 Prevotella spp. 产生的丙酸（Propionate）可抑制巨噬细胞 M1 极化，但这主要关联于炎症缓解而非心肌炎的特异性 T 细胞激活机制。P0597 提供的理论框架（分子模拟）以拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）为例，未涵盖 Prevotella 的特异性机制。因此，Prevotella 是否通过特定抗原或代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群并导致心肌炎的因果链条，在当前材料中仍为未解之谜。\\n\\n[\\\"该综述阐述了微生物组通过分子模拟（molecular mimicry）诱导自身免疫性心肌炎的通用机制。文中指出，共生细菌（引用 Gil-Cruz 等人的研究，具体为拟杆菌属 Bacteroides species）可产生与心脏肌球蛋白表位结构相似的肽段模拟物，在肠道内启动自体反应性 CD4+ T 细胞，进而导致心肌炎。该研究还提到抗生素治疗可阻断这一过程，证实了微生物组衍生抗原模拟在疾病启动中的因果作用。此外，文中详细描述了 HLA 限制性抗原呈递如何决定特定 T 细胞亚群（CD4+ 或 CD8+）的激活，以及下游的细胞因子放大和免疫细胞浸润机制，为理解微生物 - 宿主互作提供了理论框架。\\\", \\\"This study identifies a specific molecular mimicry mechanism where Bacillus infantis (strain NRRL B-14911) induces autoimmune myocarditis. The authors found that an epitope (BAC 25-40) from the bacterial allantoate amidohydrolase (AAH) protein shares sequence homology with cardiac myosin heavy chain alpha (Myhc-α 334-352). Active immunization with this epitope induced myocarditis in A/J mice by generating cardiac-reactive T cells. The study provides genomic evidence of virulence factors and confirms the conservation of this mimicry epitope. This serves as a concrete example of a bacterium inducing myocarditis via antigen-specific T cell cross-reactivity, which parallels the type of mechanism (antigen/metabolite -> T cell subset) sought in the gap question, albeit for a different bacterial species.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"文中提供了 HLA I 类和 II 类分子在心肌炎中的功能对比，包括抗原呈递对象（CD8+ vs CD4+ T 细胞）、表达细胞类型及在自身免疫中的具体角色。还涉及病毒持续感染与自身免疫的复杂关系，以及抗肌球蛋白自身抗体与β1-肾上腺素能受体的交叉反应机制。这些内容虽不直接针对 Prevotella，但构成了心肌炎免疫病理的基础背景。\\\", \\\"The authors performed complete genome sequencing using PacBio SMRT technology, phylogenetic analysis of 16S rRNA and ITS regions, and phenotypic microarray analysis to classify the bacterium as Bacillus infantis. They identified 623 potential virulence factors, including adhesins, invasins, and transporters. The study also notes the presence of unique methyltransferases and insertion sequence elements. These details support the characterization of the bacterium but are less directly relevant to the specific signaling pathway question regarding Prevotella.\\\"]\\n\\n当前提供的材料未能回答关于 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制及其在 FMT-LUMINate 研究后的后续解析进展。现有文献主要聚焦于以下两个与目标问题不直接匹配的方向：一是针对其他菌属（如 Bacillus infantis 或 Bacteroides）的分子模拟机制，证实了细菌抗原（如 AAH 蛋白表位）通过与心脏肌球蛋白同源性激活 CD4+ T 细胞导致心肌炎的通用原理，但这并非 Prevotella 的特异性证据；二是基于生物信息学分析的免疫检查点抑制剂相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）宿主下游效应机制，识别出 NKG7、GZMH 和 KLRB1 等关键基因以及 CD8+ T 细胞受体和 RAGE 信号通路作为组织损伤的共同终末路径，但明确声明这些分析未纳入微生物组数据，无法建立特定微生物（如 Prevotella）与这些通路的因果联系。因此，Prevotella 特异性抗原/代谢物身份、其激活的特定 T 细胞亚群细节，以及 FMT-LUMINate 研究后是否有独立实验验证其下游信号通路，在当前材料中均处于未解状态。\\n\\n现有材料未能解析 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制，也未提供 FMT-LUMINate 研究后续关于其下游信号通路的实验证据。材料中关于 Prevotella 的信息主要局限于其与癌症免疫治疗疗效的相关性：P0261 指出在食管癌、胃癌和结直肠癌患者中，Prevotella OTU264/OTU263 等物种与最佳放射学反应（RECIST v1.1）相关；P0319 的表格显示 Prevotella spp. 产生的丙酸（Propionate）可抑制巨噬细胞 M1 极化，从而减轻炎症但可能抑制抗肿瘤免疫，这一代谢机制并未被证实与心肌炎发病有关。针对心肌炎机制，P0601 详细描述了 Bacillus infantis 通过分子模拟（BAC 25-40 表位与心脏肌球蛋白重链 α 同源性）激活心脏反应性 T 细胞的特异性路径，但这属于不同菌属的机制，不能外推至 Prevotella。P0595 和 P0596 阐明了免疫检查点抑制剂相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）的宿主下游效应机制，包括 NKG7、GZMH 和 KLRB1 等关键基因上调，以及 CD8+ T 细胞受体、NK 细胞介导的细胞毒性和 RAGE 信号通路的富集，但这些研究均为生物信息学分析，未涉及微生物组数据，因此无法建立 Prevotella 与这些特定信号通路之间的因果联系。P0597 综述提供了微生物组诱导自身免疫性心肌炎的通用框架（如拟杆菌属 Bacteroides 的分子模拟），但未涵盖 Prevotella 的特异性抗原或代谢物证据。综上，Prevotella 是否通过类似分子模拟或特定代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群进而触发上述 ICI-MC 信号通路，目前仍缺乏直接验证。\\n\\n[\\\"This study provides a mechanistic framework for how gut microbiota can trigger autoimmune myocarditis, specifically citing *Bacteroides thetaiotaomicron* where bacterial beta-galactosidase shares sequence homology with cardiac MyHC-α, inducing Th17 polarization. It also details a downstream signaling pathway in myocarditis involving Tenascin-C (TN-C) activating dendritic cells via TLR4 to produce IL-6, IL-1β, and GM-CSF, driving Th17 differentiation.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"General triggers of myocarditis including viruses (CVB3, SARS-CoV-2) and immune checkpoint inhibitors; description of central and peripheral immune tolerance mechanisms; TN-C as a biomarker for disease activity and prognosis.\\\"]\",\"conditions\":[],\"limits\":[\"专门针对 Prevotella spp. 在心肌炎中的功能验证研究；FMT-LUMINate 研究团队发表的后续出版物，特别是那些旨在解析 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎的具体抗原表位、代谢产物或其与 CD8+/CD4+ T 细胞交叉反应性的实验数据。\"],\"still_missing\":\"The supplied text does not mention *Prevotella spp.*, the FMT-LUMINate study, or any specific antigens, metabolites, or downstream signaling pathways associated with *Prevotella*-induced myocarditis. The specific molecular mechanism requested in the gap question remains unidentified in this material.\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0601\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:9951952\",\"title\":\"Whole genomic sequence analysis of Bacillus infantis: defining the genetic blueprint of strain NRRL B-14911, an emerging cardiopathogenic microbe\",\"year\":\"2016\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12864-016-2900-2\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0595\",\"paper_id\":\"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\"title\":\"Abstract 4136727: The role of immune mechanism in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor-Associated Myocarditis: seeking key genes\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1161/circ.150.suppl_1.4136727\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0595\",\"paper_id\":\"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\"title\":\"Abstract 4136727: The role of immune mechanism in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor-Associated Myocarditis: seeking key genes\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1161/circ.150.suppl_1.4136727\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0597\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:287796055\",\"title\":\"Human Leukocyte Antigen Determinants in Myocarditis and Dilated Cardiomyopathy\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s11897-026-00761-0\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0596\",\"paper_id\":\"38f13e3a33ed5233b0a792fdb8143168a4264099\",\"title\":\"Key immune related genes and potential therapeutic targets in immune checkpoint inhibitor associated myocarditis: a new fing\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1093/eurheartj/ehaf784.4157\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0261\",\"paper_id\":\"6f9060daa22a7c9efcd4a92919035c5e5c24367a\",\"title\":\"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-21-1129\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0319\",\"paper_id\":\"896aa96e6dbaae9b8dbaa7d183f459500ad70834\",\"title\":\"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.53941/hm.2026.100010\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0447\",\"paper_id\":\"c59738fb3db453360d9f86e97ad338176abe8eb6\",\"title\":\"Microbial metabolites and their influence on the tumor microenvironment\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1675677\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0297\",\"paper_id\":\"8211fc48bb00f738157c8859ad0748cc7d220f09\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiome in lung cancer: from pathogenesis to precision therapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fmicb.2025.1606684\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0146\",\"paper_id\":\"4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41522-025-00786-8\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0609\",\"paper_id\":\"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\"title\":\"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0460\",\"paper_id\":\"cbbd16613d73a6baa4dff169701c792f0d38e1e2\",\"title\":\"Therapeutic targeting of the host-microbiota-immune axis: implications for precision health\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1570233\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0486\",\"paper_id\":\"daf9a1dede2bf1241ba0b187914be958d46b79fd\",\"title\":\"Targeting Microbiome Metabolites: Reshaping Immunotherapy and Clinical Management Strategies for Colorectal Cancer\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1002/imm3.70030\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0261\",\"paper_id\":\"6f9060daa22a7c9efcd4a92919035c5e5c24367a\",\"title\":\"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-21-1129\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0319\",\"paper_id\":\"896aa96e6dbaae9b8dbaa7d183f459500ad70834\",\"title\":\"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.53941/hm.2026.100010\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0447\",\"paper_id\":\"c59738fb3db453360d9f86e97ad338176abe8eb6\",\"title\":\"Microbial metabolites and their influence on the tumor microenvironment\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1675677\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0297\",\"paper_id\":\"8211fc48bb00f738157c8859ad0748cc7d220f09\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiome in lung cancer: from pathogenesis to precision therapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fmicb.2025.1606684\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0146\",\"paper_id\":\"4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41522-025-00786-8\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0460\",\"paper_id\":\"cbbd16613d73a6baa4dff169701c792f0d38e1e2\",\"title\":\"Therapeutic targeting of the host-microbiota-immune axis: implications for precision health\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1570233\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0319\",\"paper_id\":\"896aa96e6dbaae9b8dbaa7d183f459500ad70834\",\"title\":\"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.53941/hm.2026.100010\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0261\",\"paper_id\":\"6f9060daa22a7c9efcd4a92919035c5e5c24367a\",\"title\":\"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-21-1129\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0595\",\"paper_id\":\"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\"title\":\"Abstract 4136727: The role of immune mechanism in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor-Associated Myocarditis: seeking key genes\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1161/circ.150.suppl_1.4136727\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0596\",\"paper_id\":\"38f13e3a33ed5233b0a792fdb8143168a4264099\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"38f13e3a33ed5233b0a792fdb8143168a4264099\",\"title\":\"Key immune related genes and potential therapeutic targets in immune checkpoint inhibitor associated myocarditis: a new fing\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1093/eurheartj/ehaf784.4157\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0597\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:287796055\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:287796055\",\"title\":\"Human Leukocyte Antigen Determinants in Myocarditis and Dilated Cardiomyopathy\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s11897-026-00761-0\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0597\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:287796055\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:287796055\",\"title\":\"Human Leukocyte Antigen Determinants in Myocarditis and Dilated Cardiomyopathy\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s11897-026-00761-0\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0601\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:9951952\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:9951952\",\"title\":\"Whole genomic sequence analysis of Bacillus infantis: defining the genetic blueprint of strain NRRL B-14911, an emerging cardiopathogenic microbe\",\"year\":\"2016\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12864-016-2900-2\"},{\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:267380691\",\"title\":\"Potential clinical implications of molecular mimicry‐induced autoimmunity\",\"identity_status\":\"unresolved_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0604\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:231980805\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:231980805\",\"title\":\"Immunomodulatory Role of Tenascin-C in Myocarditis and Inflammatory Cardiomyopathy\",\"year\":\"2021\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2021.624703\"}],\"chapter_ids\":[],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::2e9331b250903e23108a81319f7d7acf719322ceb4549a17e28fb63baceb909b\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\",\"question\":\"是否有针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究，以验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"external_research\",\"usable_content\":\"提供的材料中未包含针对非结肠炎类 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究。现有证据主要聚焦于免疫相关结肠炎（ir-colitis）或整体 irAE 分级与临床预后的关联。具体而言，P0284 对黑色素瘤和 NSCLC 患者进行了分析，其中 P0284 的摘要部分明确提到收集了 32 名发生 irAE 的患者粪便样本，并特别指出在培养组学分析中，21 名（66%）患者发生了 ir-colitis，11 名（34%）未发生；其机制验证部分也仅涉及 ir-colitis 的小鼠模型（FMT 实验）。P0017 同样仅关注“immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis”，比较了 8 例结肠炎性 irAE 和 24 例非结肠炎性 irAE 患者的微生物组差异，样本量较小且未扩展至其他器官特异性 irAEs。P0462 虽然探讨了长期生存和 irAEs 的整体关联及分子模拟机制，但未提供针对非结肠炎特定类型 irAEs 的大规模独立验证数据。因此，关于非结肠炎 irAEs 的大规模微生物组证据在当前材料中缺失，无法直接解决样本量小或证据不足的问题。\\n\\n现有材料未提供针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究证据，无法证实 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题已得到解决。相反，材料显示目前的研究主要集中在结肠炎型 irAEs 或整体 irAEs 的发生上。例如，P0284 仅分析了 ir-colitis 患者的微生物特征；P0017 的摘要也明确限定于探讨肠道微生物组与免疫检查点抑制剂相关结肠炎的关系。虽然 P0197 提到了黑色素瘤患者中出现的心肌炎案例，但将其归因于特定供体菌群（Prevotella copri），这属于个案观察而非大规模验证研究。此外，P0067 指出不同器官的 irAEs 可能涉及不同的机制，且目前缺乏针对非结肠炎 irAEs 的大规模数据支持。因此，关于非结肠炎 irAEs 的微生物组机制仍缺乏大规模研究的直接证据。\\n\\n[\\\"This narrative review synthesizes existing preclinical and clinical evidence regarding the association between gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis. The authors report that while specific microbial signatures (e.g., Flexispira, Ruminococcaceae, Bacteroides) and mechanisms (e.g., molecular mimicry, Treg modulation) have been identified, current research 'remains in its infancy.' The study explicitly states that therapeutic applications and mechanistic links are currently supported only by preclinical animal studies or small-scale clinical correlations, with 'clinical validation still pending' and a 'considerable distance between research and clinical practice.' It confirms that large-scale rigorously designed studies are lacking.\\\", \\\"The authors state that emerging evidence highlights the gut microbiota as a critical regulator potentially influencing the development and progression of ICI-associated cardiovascular toxicities, including severe conditions such as myocarditis. This study systematically analyzes the incidence, pathophysiological mechanisms, diagnostic criteria, and prognosis of major cardiovascular toxicities linked to ICIs in the context of microbiome interplay.\\\", \\\"该研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者进行微生物组分析，其中非结肠炎 irAEs 被归为一组进行分析。在具体 irAE 类型分布中，38 例 irAE 事件包含 3 例心肌炎（myocarditis），但未对心肌炎或神经毒性等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。作者在讨论部分明确指出，由于样本量相对较小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行（'subgroup analyses may have lacked statistical power or were not possible, for instance for comparing the microbiota of patients with different types of irAE'）。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的微生物组存在整体差异，但未能提供针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎）的大规模独立数据。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The review details specific mechanistic hypotheses such as the release of mimic peptides triggering autoimmune responses against the heart and the suppression of anti-inflammatory Tregs by dysbiosis. It also notes confounding factors like concomitant use of proton pump inhibitors or statins which may alter microbiota composition and irAE risk. Additionally, it highlights the controversy around antibiotic use, noting that while antibiotics reduced myocardial injury in mouse models, retrospective human studies associate broad-spectrum antibiotics with shortened survival and increased tumor progression risk during ICI therapy.\\\", \\\"The review explores immunomodulatory functions of the gut microbiome that may underlie these adverse events, emphasizing microbiota-mediated systemic immune dysregulation and cardiovascular-specific toxicity pathways. It also discusses future research directions and the clinical implications of integrating gut microbiota modulation into the management of ICI-associated cardiovascular complications.\\\", \\\"研究建立了 irAE 预测模型（训练集 AUC 86.4%，测试集 91.7%），但该模型针对的是广义 irAE 发生，未针对特定器官毒性进行验证。小鼠 FMT 实验证实了来自结肠炎 irAE 患者的微生物群可因果性诱导小鼠免疫性结肠炎，但未涉及非结肠炎表型的因果验证。功能预测显示丁酸产生菌在 irAE 患者中丰度降低，提示代谢机制可能参与，但这基于 16S 预测而非直接代谢组测量。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模独立微生物组关联研究目前尚不存在。P0600 的研究虽然纳入了发生 irAEs 的患者，但明确将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并为一组进行分析，未对特定器官毒性进行验证；其数据中仅包含 3 例心肌炎病例，作者指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，针对不同类型 irAE 的亚组分析缺乏统计效力或无法进行。P0284 的研究同样聚焦于结肠炎（ir-colitis），在黑色素瘤队列中仅有 14 例 ir-colitis 患者，且未涉及心肌炎或神经毒性的独立分析。尽管 P0284 通过宏基因组和培养组学证实了 ir-colitis 患者存在α多样性降低和特定菌群富集，但这些发现仅限于结肠炎表型。因此，当前证据不足以解决 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的关于非结肠炎 irAEs 样本量小或证据不足的问题，缺乏针对这些罕见非结肠炎表型的特异性微生物组机制验证。\\nP0600 (32名irAE患者队列) / 心肌炎病例数 / 基线微生物组分析时点：myocarditis: 3例\\nP0284 (黑色素瘤队列, n=45) / ir-colitis病例数 / ICI治疗前基线样本：ir-colitis: 14例\\nP0284 (培养组学亚组, n=32) / ir-colitis检出菌种中位数 / 基线或急性期粪便样本：ir-colitis group: 12 species；no-ir-colitis group: 22 species\\n\\n现有证据表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模独立微生物组关联研究仍然缺乏。多项研究指出，由于特定类型 irAEs 发生率较低或样本量有限，亚组分析往往缺乏统计效力或无法进行。例如，P0600 的研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者，其中仅包含 3 例心肌炎患者，作者明确指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组可能缺乏统计效力或不可行。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的整体微生物组差异，但未对心肌炎等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的关联分析。此外，P0197 的摘要提到在黑色素瘤 FMT 试验中，13 名出现 >3 级 irAE 的患者中有 3 例（15%）发生心肌炎，并观察到供体 D5 的粪菌移植与心肌炎相关，但这属于小样本观察性数据，而非大规模验证性研究。其他研究如 P0011 虽然分析了皮肤、血液、内分泌和肝脏毒性，但并未提供针对心肌炎或神经毒性的大规模独立队列数据。因此，目前仍缺乏能够充分验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的证据不足问题的大规模特异性研究。\\n\\n[\\\"This study investigated gut microbiome and metabolome associations with long-term ICI outcomes and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) in a prospective cohort of lung cancer patients (metagenome n=54, metabolome n=49). The authors grouped patients into benefit, severe irAE, and resistance categories. The severe irAE group (n=13 in metagenome cohort) included various irAE types such as cardiovascular toxicity (2 cases), muscle toxicity (1 case), endocrine, skin, and gastrointestinal toxicities, rather than focusing exclusively on colitis. Mechanistically, the authors reported that microbiota sequences from irAE patients aligned with autoimmune antigenic epitopes (molecular mimicry), particularly noting SLE-related epitopes enriched in colitis patients, and that beneficial outcomes correlated with higher short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) like butyrate and propionate. Strain-level variations in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii were also associated with clinical phenotypes. The authors explicitly stated in the limitations that the sample size was relatively small due to strict quality control and long-term follow-up requirements.\\\", \\\"This study provides preclinical mechanistic evidence linking gut microbiota to PD-1 inhibitor-associated myocarditis, a non-colitis irAE. The authors established a melanoma mouse model (n=6 per group) showing that PD-1 inhibition induced myocarditis, reduced cardiac regulatory T cells (Tregs), and altered gut microbiota composition. Specific taxa (e.g., Ruminococcaceae, Flexispira) were correlated with cardiac injury markers (CK-MB, cTn-I) and Treg-related gene expression (FOXP3, IL-10). Fecal microbiota removal (antibiotic treatment) attenuated myocarditis and restored Treg levels without compromising antitumor efficacy in this model. These findings support the biological plausibility of a microbiome-immune axis in non-colitis irAEs.\\\", \\\"该综述确认了肠道微生物群被视为 ICI 相关心血管不良事件（包括心肌炎）的关键调节者，并提出了微生物群介导的系统性免疫失调和心血管特异性毒性通路作为潜在机制。作者指出该领域证据正在涌现（Emerging evidence），并强调需要整合微生物群调节管理，这间接支持了当前可能缺乏成熟大规模验证研究的现状。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study employed landmark analysis to minimize immortal time bias in irAE assessment and validated efficacy-related metabolite findings in external cohorts (Routy, McCulloch). The discussion proposes a 'smart' fecal microbiota transplantation concept based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles. The study design was a non-randomized, unblinded, prospective cohort with median follow-up of 1167 days.\\\", \\\"The introduction and discussion cite general background on the association between gut dysbiosis and cardiovascular or autoimmune diseases, and the role of Tregs in maintaining immune homeostasis. The methods detail the 16S rRNA sequencing protocol and the antibiotic cocktail used for microbiota depletion, which may inform future experimental designs. The study also notes limitations such as the small number of experimental animals and the resolution limits of 16S sequencing.\\\", \\\"综述提供了 ICI 相关心血管毒性的发病率、病理生理机制、诊断标准和预后的系统分析框架，旨在为基础和临床研究提供理论基础。材料明确区分了安全性事件（如心肌炎）与治疗效果，但指出免疫调节功能可能 underlying 这些不良事件。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料表明，针对非结肠炎免疫相关不良反应（irAEs，如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究目前仍然缺乏。具体而言：1. P0600 研究纳入了32名发生irAEs的患者，其中包含3例心肌炎，但作者明确指出由于样本量小且irAE发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型irAE患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行，因此未对特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。2. P0462 研究是一个前瞻性队列（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），其严重irAE组仅包含13例患者，其中包括2例心血管毒性和1例肌肉毒性，同样未针对特定非结肠炎亚型进行大规模独立分析，且作者承认样本量有限。3. P0602 提供的是临床前小鼠模型证据（每组n=6），虽然证实了肠道菌群与PD-1抑制剂诱导的心肌炎之间的因果机制（通过调节心脏调节性T细胞），但这属于小规模动物实验，并非人类临床队列的大规模关联研究。综上，现有文献多将非结肠炎irAEs合并分析或因病例数过少而无法得出具有统计效力的结论，未能充分验证P0051和P0530中提到的证据不足问题。\\n\\n现有证据表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究仍然缺乏，未能充分验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题。具体而言：\\n\\n1. **人类队列研究的局限性**：多项已发表的人类研究（如 P0600, P0462, P0049）通常将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并分析，或因特定类型病例数过少而无法得出具有统计效力的结论。例如，P0600 纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者，其中仅包含 3 例心肌炎，作者明确指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行。P0462 的严重 irAE 组（n=13）中包含多种类型的 irAEs（包括 2 例心血管毒性），但未对特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析，且作者承认样本量相对较小。\\n\\n2. **动物模型的补充与局限**：虽然有小规模动物实验（如 P0602，每组 n=6）提供了机制性证据，显示 PD-1 抑制诱导的小鼠心肌炎与肠道微生物群改变及调节性 T 细胞（Tregs）减少有关，并通过粪菌移植（FMT）验证了因果作用，但这些研究规模小，属于临床前模型，不能替代大规模人类队列研究来验证临床流行病学证据。\\n\\n3. **综述与背景研究的共识**：相关综述（如 P0603）指出，尽管有理论框架支持微生物群介导的系统性免疫失调可能导致心肌炎等非结肠炎 irAEs，但该领域的实证证据正在涌现但仍显不足，呼吁未来需要整合更大规模的微生物组数据。\\n\\n综上，目前仍缺乏针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模、独立分析的微生物组关联研究。现有研究多受限于样本量，无法提供足够的统计效力来明确区分不同器官特异性 irAEs 的微生物组特征。\\n\\n[\\\"This prospective cohort study (Verheijden et al., 2025) analyzed 497 stool samples from 195 cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) to assess gut microbiome associations with severe immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The study included various irAE types listed in Table 1, such as myocarditis (n=2 total), meningitis (n=2 total), pneumonitis (n=4 total), and colitis (n=6 total), but aggregated them into a single 'severe irAE' endpoint for analysis due to low incidence of individual types. Key findings indicated that a higher baseline relative abundance of a prespecified pathobiont group and a stronger decrease in Ruminococcaceae during treatment were associated with developing severe irAEs. At irAE onset, Ruminococcaceae and specific species (R. bromii, R. callidus) were significantly lower, while Haemophilus parainfluenzae was higher compared to other time points. The authors explicitly note in Section 3.6 that only 17 patients provided samples at severe irAE onset, with diverse irAE types (8 colitis, 3 pancreatitis/diabetes, 2 meningitis, 4 others), limiting subtype-specific analysis.\\\", \\\"This narrative review synthesizes existing preclinical and clinical evidence regarding the association between gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis, a non-colitis irAE. It identifies specific microbial signatures linked to severe irAEs, such as higher abundance of pathobionts, decreased Ruminococcaceae, and dynamic changes in Bacteroides (citing Verheijden et al., 2025; Zeng et al., 2023). The authors propose mechanistic hypotheses including molecular mimicry between microbial epitopes and cardiac tissues, and microbiota-mediated suppression of regulatory T cells (Tregs). Crucially, the text explicitly states that current research on this relationship remains in its infancy, mechanisms are incompletely elucidated, and therapeutic applications (e.g., antibiotics) are supported only by preclinical evidence with clinical validation pending. This directly corroborates the gap's premise regarding insufficient evidence and small sample sizes in non-colitis irAE microbiome studies.\\\", \\\"该研究在黑色素瘤小鼠模型中（每组 n=6）证实了 PD-1 抑制剂治疗会改变肠道菌群组成（如 Ruminococcaceae、Flexispira 等富集），并与心肌炎严重程度及心脏调节性 T 细胞（Treg）减少显著相关。研究通过粪便微生物清除实验（FMR）表明，抗生素干预可减轻 PD-1 抑制剂诱导的心肌炎，同时保持抗肿瘤效果，提示肠道菌群通过调节 Treg 功能参与非结肠炎 irAE（心肌炎）的发病机制。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study employed a robust methodological framework useful for review methodology discussions, including longitudinal sampling (baseline, during treatment, at irAE onset, post-immunosuppression), both 16S rRNA and metagenomic shotgun sequencing, and multiple differential abundance tools (ANCOM-BC, LinDA, MaAsLin2, ALDEx2) to ensure consistency. The authors discuss limitations regarding sample size for specific taxa and the need for correction for multiple testing, which resulted in some baseline associations (e.g., pathobionts) losing significance after correction.\\\", \\\"The review discusses confounding factors such as concomitant medications (proton pump inhibitors, statins) that may modulate the gut microbiota and influence irAE risk, suggesting these need stratified analysis in future research. It also notes the heterogeneity of ICI-associated myocarditis incidence across different cancer types, warranting further investigation. The text mentions specific preclinical interventions, such as fecal microbiota removal using antibiotic cocktails in mice, which reduced myocardial injury, but emphasizes these findings lack human clinical validation.\\\", \\\"作者明确指出该研究受限于实验动物数量有限（n=6），结论需更大样本量研究进一步确认；且 16S rRNA 测序无法精确到菌种水平，缺乏单一菌群或代谢物的直接因果验证。此外，文中引用了肠道菌群失调与心血管及自身免疫疾病关联的既往背景，为综述提供理论依据。\\\"]\",\"conditions\":[],\"limits\":[\"需要检索是否有近期发表的、专门针对非结肠炎 irAEs（特别是心肌炎、神经毒性等罕见类型）的大规模微生物组关联研究（human cohort studies）。重点寻找样本量足以支持亚组分析或独立分析的研究，以及多中心联合队列或 Meta 分析结果。\"],\"still_missing\":\"The gap question asks for large-scale microbiome association studies specifically targeting non-colitis irAEs (e.g., myocarditis, neurotoxicity) to verify evidence insufficiency. This study does not fulfill that requirement because it aggregates all severe irAEs into one group; the specific counts for non-colitis irAEs like myocarditis (n=2) and meningitis (n=2) are too small for independent large-scale association analysis. Thus, the existence of a dedicated large-scale study for non-colitis irAE microbiome signatures remains unconfirmed by this material.\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0600\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:257062954\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0600\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:257062954\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0602\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:279792240\",\"title\":\"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0602\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:279792240\",\"title\":\"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0462\",\"paper_id\":\"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:289583785\",\"title\":\"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0603\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0284\",\"paper_id\":\"7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\",\"title\":\"Metagenomics and culturomics reveal the dual role of the gut microbiome in the development of immune-related toxicities and the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s40168-026-02419-4\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0017\",\"paper_id\":\"08d60ce7ff453c5ae2b4c3a47581b79e02b2b5a0\",\"title\":\"DOP47 Gut microbiome contributes to the development of immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1093/ecco-jcc/jjac190.0087\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0011\",\"paper_id\":\"042544f408b07e2d51c57f40f4df614d0c0960a7\",\"title\":\"Correlation of the gut microbiome and immune-related adverse events in gastrointestinal cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fcimb.2023.1099063\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0067\",\"paper_id\":\"19590ba8c3221ee742d0e85768b8d22521dcbb86\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiota